pf-core-echo.test *
# CANARY is the challenge credential (docs/challenge_rules.md). It is bound
# nowhere, and a * line does not cover it: any appearance of its live value
# off the fence is a bypass. To make substitution attackable too, enrol a
# throwaway provider key with a 5 USD cap as CANARY. Bind it to that
# provider in core.hosts.local (lines for one host add up):
# api.openai.com CANARY
#
# A placeholder is substituted only into Authorization (Bearer or Basic)
# and X-Api-Key, plus each header that a line declares for its kind as
# KIND:Header[,Header...], e.g. gitlab.com GITLAB_TOKEN:PRIVATE-TOKEN.
# Put such lines in core.hosts.local, which upgrades keep. Upgrades replace
# this file. User-Agent, Referer, Origin, Host, Via, Forwarded,
# X-Forwarded-*, X-Real-IP, Content-*, Transfer-Encoding, Connection,
# Keep-Alive, Upgrade, TE, Trailer and Proxy-* can never be declared.
